menu "USV GPS simulator"

    config USV_GPS_WIFI_SSID
        string "Wi-Fi SSID to join"
        default "usv-bench"
        help
            Station SSID.  The simulator joins this network when it is in range
            and prints its IP on the USB console; the softAP stays available as
            a fallback either way.

    config USV_GPS_WIFI_PASSWORD
        string "Wi-Fi password"
        default "usv12345"
        help
            Station password.  Must be at least 8 characters for WPA2.

    config USV_GPS_AP_SSID
        string "Fallback softAP SSID"
        default "USV-GPS-SIM"
        help
            SSID of the access point the simulator always raises.  Connect to it
            and browse http://192.168.4.1 when the bench network is unavailable.

    config USV_GPS_AP_PASSWORD
        string "Fallback softAP password"
        default "usvgps123"
        help
            Access point password, minimum 8 characters.

    config USV_GPS_MON_TX_GPIO
        int "Monitor UART TX GPIO (-1 disables)"
        range -1 21
        default 7
        help
            Optional transmit-only mirror of the NMEA stream, so a USB-TTL probe
            can watch the sentences the flight controller is receiving without
            unplugging anything.  GPIO7 is free on ESP32-C3 modules.

    config USV_GPS_LED_GPIO
        int "Blue LED GPIO (-1 disables)"
        range -1 21
        default 8
        help
            GPIO of the on-board blue LED.  Most ESP32-C3 SuperMini boards wire
            it to GPIO8 with the anode to 3V3 (active low); some devkits use a
            different pin or the opposite polarity.  Set -1 to disable blinking
            entirely, or change the polarity option below if the LED stays on
            instead of blinking.

    config USV_GPS_LED_ACTIVE_LOW
        bool "LED is active low (lit when the pin is driven to 0)"
        default y
        help
            Suits the common C3 SuperMini wiring where the LED anode goes to
            3V3 and the cathode to the GPIO.  Turn this off for boards that
            light the LED when the pin is high.

    config USV_GPS_LED_PULSE_MS
        int "LED pulse width in milliseconds"
        range 2 500
        default 20
        help
            How long the LED stays lit per NMEA burst.  Keep it well under the
            output period or consecutive pulses will merge and the LED will look
            solid.  At the default 5 Hz (200 ms) a 20 ms pulse gives a clearly
            separate flash five times a second.

endmenu